fter `create-table` and `drop-table`.\n- **`datasette/write_sql.py`:** `create view` now requires `create-view` on the database. `drop view` requires `drop-view` on the view, as a table resource.\n- **`datasette/utils/sql_analysis.py`:** I renamed `dropped_tables` to `dropped_tables_and_views` and made it include dropped views. SQLite's spurious delete on a dropped view's name is now suppressed, so it doesn't become a `delete-row` requirement.\n- **`docs/authentication.rst`:** I added both actions to the `--root` permissions list and gave each its own action section.", "ttft_ms": 2583, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 40654, "uuid": "c448a39f-4dc9-4034-be36-d51b4697f48e", "ttft_stream_ms": 2134, "time_to_request_ms": 50, "first_content_frame_ms": 2134, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
